# TASK: Secure MCP Configuration + Add PostgreSQL MCP Server

## Context

`.cursor/mcp.json` currently contains 3 MCP servers (context7, playwright, filesystem).
We need to add PostgreSQL MCP and secure the config since it will now contain database credentials.

This is an infrastructure task. No application code changes.

---

## Step 1 — Add `.cursor/mcp.json` to `.gitignore`

File: `.gitignore`

Add this line:

```
.cursor/mcp.json
```

Reason: the file will now contain database credentials (DATABASE_URL with password). Credentials must never be committed to git (MASTER_SPEC §13.2).

---

## Step 2 — Create `.cursor/mcp.json.example`

File: `.cursor/mcp.json.example`

This is the template for the team — committed to git, no secrets:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "context7": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@upstash/context7-mcp@latest"]
    },
    "playwright": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@playwright/mcp@latest"]
    },
    "filesystem": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "-y",
        "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem",
        "/absolute/path/to/indai-clean-website"
      ]
    },
    "postgres": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "-y",
        "@modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres",
        "DATABASE_URL_FROM_ENV_LOCAL"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

---

## Step 3 — Update `.cursor/mcp.json` with PostgreSQL

File: `.cursor/mcp.json`

Add the postgres server to the existing config. Keep all 3 existing servers, add this one:

```json
"postgres": {
  "command": "npx",
  "args": [
    "-y",
    "@modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres",
    "postgresql://gen_user:ПАРОЛЬ@ХОСТ:5432/default_db?sslmode=require"
  ]
}
```

Replace `ПАРОЛЬ` and `ХОСТ` with the real values from `.env.local` DATABASE_URL.

⚠️ Use `sslmode=require` (NOT `verify-full`) — unless a CA certificate is explicitly configured.

---

## Step 4 — Verify `.env.local` has DATABASE_URL

File: `.env.local`

Confirm that `DATABASE_URL` is set with the same connection string.
Confirm `.env.local` is in `.gitignore` (MASTER_SPEC §13.2).

---

## Step 5 — Verify `.env.example` has DATABASE_URL key

File: `.env.example`

Confirm it contains (no value, just the key — §13.2):

```
DATABASE_URL=
```

---

## Verification

- [ ] `.cursor/mcp.json` contains all 4 servers (context7, playwright, filesystem, postgres)
- [ ] `.cursor/mcp.json` is in `.gitignore`
- [ ] `.cursor/mcp.json.example` exists and is committed (no secrets)
- [ ] `.env.local` has DATABASE_URL
- [ ] `.env.local` is in `.gitignore`
- [ ] `.env.example` has DATABASE_URL key (no value)
- [ ] Restart Cursor and verify postgres server appears in Settings → Tools and Integration
